175476	175679	175447	175447	Warrington	1404	“ As rogues of note in former days who had some wicked work to perform,—an enemy to be put out of the way , a quantity of false coin to be passed , a lie to be told or a murder to be done — employed a professional perjurer or assassin to do the work , which they were themselves too notorious or too cowardly to execute : our notorious contemporary , the Day , engages smashers out of doors to utter forgeries against individuals , and calls in auxiliary cut - throats to murder the reputation of those who offend him . A black - vizarded ruffian ( whom we will unmask ) , who signs the forged name of Trefoil , is at present one of the chief bravoes and bullies in our contemporary ’s establishment . He is the eunuch who brings the bowstring , and strangles at the order of the Day . We can convict this cowardly slave , and propose to do so . The charge which he has brought against Lord Bangbanagher , because he is a Liberal Irish peer , and against the Board of Poor Law Guardians of the Bangbanagher Union , is , ”
